-- NRSV-CE OLD TESTAMENT BIBLE VERSES (PART 3)


When we had headed out along the route of the wilderness of Moab,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 9, 'the LORD said to me: "Do not harass Moab or engage them in battle, for I will not give you any of its land as a possession, since I have given Ar as a possession to the descendants of Lot."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 10, '(The Emim--a large and numerous people, as tall as the Anakim--had formerly inhabited it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 11, 'Like the Anakim, they are usually reckoned as Rephaim, though the Moabites call them Emim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 12, 'Moreover, the Horim had formerly inhabited Seir, but the descendants of Esau dispossessed them, destroying them and settling in their place, as Israel has done in the land that the LORD gave them as a possession.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 13, '"Now then, proceed to cross over the Wadi Zered."
So we crossed over the Wadi Zered.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 14, 'And the length of time we had traveled from Kadesh-barnea until we crossed the Wadi Zered was thirty-eight years, until the entire generation of warriors had perished from the camp, as the LORD had sworn concerning them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 15, 'Indeed, the LORD"s own hand was against them, to root them out from the camp, until all had perished.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 16, 'Just as soon as all the warriors had died off from among the people,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 17, 'the LORD spoke to me, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 18, '"Today you are going to cross the boundary of Moab at Ar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 19, 'When you approach the frontier of the Ammonites, do not harass them or engage them in battle, for I will not give the land of the Ammonites to you as a possession, because I have given it to the descendants of Lot."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 20, '(It also is usually reckoned as a land of Rephaim. Rephaim formerly inhabited it, though the Ammonites call them Zamzummim,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 21, 'a strong and numerous people, as tall as the Anakim. But the LORD destroyed them from before the Ammonites so that they could dispossess them and settle in their place.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 22, 'He did the same for the descendants of Esau, who live in Seir, by destroying the Horim before them so that they could dispossess them and settle in their place even to this day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 23, 'As for the Avvim, who had lived in settlements in the vicinity of Gaza, the Caphtorim, who came from Caphtor, destroyed them and settled in their place.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 24, '"Proceed on your journey and cross the Wadi Arnon. See, I have handed over to you King Sihon the Amorite of Heshbon, and his land. Begin to take possession by engaging him in battle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 25, 'This day I will begin to put the dread and fear of you upon the peoples everywhere under heaven; when they hear report of you, they will tremble and be in anguish because of you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 26, 'So I sent messengers from the wilderness of Kedemoth to King Sihon of Heshbon with the following terms of peace:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Defeat of King Sihon'),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 27, '"If you let me pass through your land, I will travel only along the road; I will turn aside neither to the right nor to the left.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 28, 'You shall sell me food for money, so that I may eat, and supply me water for money, so that I may drink. Only allow me to pass through on foot--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 29, 'just as the descendants of Esau who live in Seir have done for me and likewise the Moabites who live in Ar--until I cross the Jordan into the land that the LORD our God is giving us."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 30, 'But King Sihon of Heshbon was not willing to let us pass through, for the LORD your God had hardened his spirit and made his heart defiant in order to hand him over to you, as he has now done.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 31, 'The LORD said to me, "See, I have begun to give Sihon and his land over to you. Begin now to take possession of his land."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 32, 'So when Sihon came out against us, he and all his people for battle at Jahaz,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 33, 'the LORD our God gave him over to us; and we struck him down, along with his offspring and all his people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 34, 'At that time we captured all his towns, and in each town we utterly destroyed men, women, and children. We left not a single survivor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 35, 'Only the livestock we kept as spoil for ourselves, as well as the plunder of the towns that we had captured.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 36, 'From Aroer on the edge of the Wadi Arnon (including the town that is in the wadi itself) as far as Gilead, there was no citadel too high for us. The LORD our God gave everything to us.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 2, 37, 'You did not encroach, however, on the land of the Ammonites, avoiding the whole upper region of the Wadi Jabbok as well as the towns of the hill country, just as the LORD our God had charged.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



Hear, O Israel, the statutes and ordinances that I am addressing to you today; you shall learn them and observe them diligently.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Ten Commandments'),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 2, 'The LORD our God made a covenant with us at Horeb.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 3, 'Not with our ancestors did the LORD make this covenant, but with us, who are all of us here alive today.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 4, 'The LORD spoke with you face to face at the mountain, out of the fire.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 5, '(At that time I was standing between the LORD and you to declare to you the words of the LORD; for you were afraid because of the fire and did not go up the mountain.) And he said:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 6, 'I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 7, 'you shall have no other gods before me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 8, 'You shall not make for yourself an idol, whether in the form of anything that is in heaven above, or that is on the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 9, 'You shall not bow down to them or worship them; for I the LORD your God am a jealous God, punishing children for the iniquity of parents, to the third and fourth generation of those who reject me,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 10, 'but showing steadfast love to the thousandth generation of those who love me and keep my commandments.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 11, 'You shall not make wrongful use of the name of the LORD your God, for the LORD will not acquit anyone who misuses his name.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 12, 'Observe the sabbath day and keep it holy, as the LORD your God commanded you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 13, 'Six days you shall labor and do all your work.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 14, 'But the seventh day is a sabbath to the LORD your God; you shall not do any work--you, or your son or your daughter, or your male or female slave, or your ox or your donkey, or any of your livestock, or the resident alien in your towns, so that your male and female slave may rest as well as you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 15, 'Remember that you were a slave in the land of Egypt, and the LORD your God brought you out from there with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm; therefore the LORD your God commanded you to keep the sabbath day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 16, 'Honor your father and your mother, as the LORD your God commanded you, so that your days may be long and that it may go well with you in the land that the LORD your God is giving you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 17, 'You shall not murder.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 18, 'Neither shall you commit adultery.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 19, 'Neither shall you steal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 20, 'Neither shall you bear false witness against your neighbor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 21, 'Neither shall you covet your neighbor"s wife.
Neither shall you desire your neighbor"s house, or field, or male or female slave, or ox, or donkey, or anything that belongs to your neighbor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 22, 'These words the LORD spoke with a loud voice to your whole assembly at the mountain, out of the fire, the cloud, and the thick darkness, and he added no more. He wrote them on two stone tablets, and gave them to me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Moses the Mediator of God"s Will'),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 23, 'When you heard the voice out of the darkness, while the mountain was burning with fire, you approached me, all the heads of your tribes and your elders;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 24, 'and you said, "Look, the LORD our God has shown us his glory and greatness, and we have heard his voice out of the fire. Today we have seen that God may speak to someone and the person may still live.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 25, 'So now why should we die? For this great fire will consume us; if we hear the voice of the LORD our God any longer, we shall die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 26, 'For who is there of all flesh that has heard the voice of the living God speaking out of fire, as we have, and remained alive?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 27, 'Go near, you yourself, and hear all that the LORD our God will say. Then tell us everything that the LORD our God tells you, and we will listen and do it."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 28, 'The LORD heard your words when you spoke to me, and the LORD said to me: "I have heard the words of this people, which they have spoken to you; they are right in all that they have spoken.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 29, 'If only they had such a mind as this, to fear me and to keep all my commandments always, so that it might go well with them and with their children forever!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 30, 'Go say to them, "Return to your tents."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 31, 'But you, stand here by me, and I will tell you all the commandments, the statutes and the ordinances, that you shall teach them, so that they may do them in the land that I am giving them to possess."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 32, 'You must therefore be careful to do as the LORD your God has commanded you; you shall not turn to the right or to the left.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 5, 33, 'You must follow exactly the path that the LORD your God has commanded you, so that you may live, and that it may go well with you, and that you may live long in the land that you are to possess.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);









You shall not boil a kid in its mother"s milk.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 22, 'Set apart a tithe of all the yield of your seed that is brought in yearly from the field.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Regulations concerning Tithes'),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 23, 'In the presence of the LORD your God, in the place that he will choose as a dwelling for his name, you shall eat the tithe of your grain, your wine, and your oil, as well as the firstlings of your herd and flock, so that you may learn to fear the LORD your God always.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 24, 'But if, when the LORD your God has blessed you, the distance is so great that you are unable to transport it, because the place where the LORD your God will choose to set his name is too far away from you,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 25, 'then you may turn it into money. With the money secure in hand, go to the place that the LORD your God will choose;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 26, 'spend the money for whatever you wish--oxen, sheep, wine, strong drink, or whatever you desire. And you shall eat there in the presence of the LORD your God, you and your household rejoicing together.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 27, 'As for the Levites resident in your towns, do not neglect them, because they have no allotment or inheritance with you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 28, 'Every third year you shall bring out the full tithe of your produce for that year, and store it within your towns;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 14, 29, 'the Levites, because they have no allotment or inheritance with you, as well as the resident aliens, the orphans, and the widows in your towns, may come and eat their fill so that the LORD your God may bless you in all the work that you undertake.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

You shall do the same with regard to your female slave.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 15, 18, 'Do not consider it a hardship when you send them out from you free persons, because for six years they have given you services worth the wages of hired laborers; and the LORD your God will bless you in all that you do.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 15, 19, 'Every firstling male born of your herd and flock you shall consecrate to the LORD your God; you shall not do work with your firstling ox nor shear the firstling of your flock.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Firstborn of Livestock'),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 15, 20, 'You shall eat it, you together with your household, in the presence of the LORD your God year by year at the place that the LORD will choose.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 15, 21, 'But if it has any defect--any serious defect, such as lameness or blindness--you shall not sacrifice it to the LORD your God;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 15, 22, 'within your towns you may eat it, the unclean and the clean alike, as you would a gazelle or deer.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 15, 23, 'Its blood, however, you must not eat; you shall pour it out on the ground like water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

















    let the earth hear the words of my mouth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 2, 'May my teaching drop like the rain,  
    my speech condense like the dew;  
like gentle rain on grass,  
    like showers on new growth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 3, 'For I will proclaim the name of the LORD;  
    ascribe greatness to our God!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 4, 'The Rock, his work is perfect,  
    and all his ways are just.  
A faithful God, without deceit,  
    just and upright is he;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 5, 'yet his degenerate children have dealt falsely with him,  
    a perverse and crooked generation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 6, 'Do you thus repay the LORD,  
    O foolish and senseless people?  
Is not he your father, who created you,  
    who made you and established you?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 7, 'Remember the days of old,  
    consider the years long past;  
ask your father, and he will inform you;  
    your elders, and they will tell you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 8, 'When the Most High apportioned the nations,  
    when he divided humankind,  
he fixed the boundaries of the peoples  
    according to the number of the gods;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 9, 'the LORD"s own portion was his people,  
    Jacob his allotted share.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 10, 'He sustained him in a desert land,  
    in a howling wilderness waste;  
he shielded him, cared for him,  
    guarded him as the apple of his eye.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 11, 'As an eagle stirs up its nest,  
    and hovers over its young;  
as it spreads its wings, takes them up,  
    and bears them aloft on its pinions,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 12, 'the LORD alone guided him;  
    no foreign god was with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 13, 'He set him atop the heights of the land,  
    and fed him with produce of the field;  
he nursed him with honey from the crags,  
    with oil from flinty rock;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 14, 'curds from the herd, and milk from the flock,  
    with fat of lambs and rams;  
Bashan bulls and goats,  
    together with the choicest wheat--  
    you drank fine wine from the blood of grapes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 15, 'Jacob ate his fill;  
    Jeshurun grew fat, and kicked.  
    You grew fat, bloated, and gorged!  
He abandoned God who made him,  
    and scoffed at the Rock of his salvation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 16, 'They made him jealous with strange gods,  
    with abhorrent things they provoked him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 17, 'They sacrificed to demons, not God,  
    to deities they had never known,  
to new ones recently arrived,  
    whom your ancestors had not feared.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 18, 'You were unmindful of the Rock that bore you;  
    you forgot the God who gave you birth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 19, 'The LORD saw it, and was jealous;  
    he spurned his sons and daughters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 20, 'He said: I will hide my face from them,  
    I will see what their end will be;  
for they are a perverse generation,  
    children in whom there is no faithfulness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 21, 'They made me jealous with what is no god,  
    provoked me with their idols.  
So I will make them jealous with what is no people,  
    provoke them with a foolish nation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 22, 'For a fire is kindled by my anger,  
    and burns to the depths of Sheol;  
it devours the earth and its increase,  
    and sets on fire the foundations of the mountains.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 23, 'I will heap disasters upon them,  
    spend my arrows against them:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 24, 'wasting hunger,  
    burning consumption,  
    bitter pestilence.  
The teeth of beasts I will send against them,  
    with venom of things crawling in the dust.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 25, 'In the street the sword shall bereave,  
    and in the chambers terror,  
for young man and woman alike,  
    nursing child and old gray head.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 26, 'I thought to scatter them  
    and blot out the memory of them from humankind;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 27, 'but I feared provocation by the enemy,  
    for their adversaries might misunderstand  
and say, "Our hand is triumphant;  
    it was not the LORD who did all this."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 28, 'They are a nation void of sense;  
    there is no understanding in them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 29, 'If they were wise, they would understand this;  
    they would discern what the end would be.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 30, 'How could one have routed a thousand,  
    and two put a myriad to flight,  
unless their Rock had sold them,  
    the LORD had given them up?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 31, 'Indeed their rock is not like our Rock;  
    our enemies are fools.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 32, 'Their vine comes from the vinestock of Sodom,  
    from the vineyards of Gomorrah;  
their grapes are grapes of poison,  
    their clusters are bitter;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 33, 'their wine is the poison of serpents,  
    the cruel venom of asps.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 34, 'Is not this laid up in store with me,  
    sealed up in my treasuries?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 35, 'Vengeance is mine, and recompense,  
    for the time when their foot shall slip;  
because the day of their calamity is at hand,  
    their doom comes swiftly.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 36, 'Indeed the LORD will vindicate his people,  
    have compassion on his servants,  
when he sees that their power is gone,  
    neither bond nor free remaining.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 37, 'Then he will say: Where are their gods,  
    the rock in which they took refuge,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 38, 'who ate the fat of their sacrifices,  
    and drank the wine of their libations?  
Let them rise up and help you,  
    let them be your protection!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 39, 'See now that I, even I, am he;  
    there is no god besides me.  
I kill and I make alive;  
    I wound and I heal;  
    and no one can deliver from my hand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 40, 'For I lift up my hand to heaven,  
    and swear: As I live forever,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 41, 'when I whet my flashing sword,  
    and my hand takes hold on judgment;  
I will take vengeance on my adversaries,  
    and will repay those who hate me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 42, 'I will make my arrows drunk with blood,  
    and my sword shall devour flesh--  
with the blood of the slain and the captives,  
    from the long-haired enemy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 43, 'Praise, O heavens, his people,  
    worship him, all you gods!  
For he will avenge the blood of his children,  
    and take vengeance on his adversaries;  
he will repay those who hate him,  
    and cleanse the land for his people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 44, 'Moses came and recited all the words of this song in the hearing of the people, he and Joshua son of Nun.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 45, 'When Moses had finished reciting all these words to all Israel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 46, 'he said to them: "Take to heart all the words that I am giving in witness against you today; give them as a command to your children, so that they may diligently observe all the words of this law.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 47, 'This is no trifling matter for you, but rather your very life; through it you may live long in the land that you are crossing over the Jordan to possess."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 48, 'On that very day the LORD addressed Moses as follows:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Moses" Death Foretold'),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 49, '"Ascend this mountain of the Abarim, Mount Nebo, which is in the land of Moab, across from Jericho, and view the land of Canaan, which I am giving to the Israelites for a possession;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 50, 'you shall die there on the mountain that you ascend and shall be gathered to your kin, as your brother Aaron died on Mount Hor and was gathered to his kin;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 51, 'because both of you broke faith with me among the Israelites at the waters of Meribath-kadesh in the wilderness of Zin, by failing to maintain my holiness among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 32, 52, 'Although you may view the land from a distance, you shall not enter it--the land that I am giving to the Israelites."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

The LORD came from Sinai,  
    and dawned from Seir upon us;  
    he shone forth from Mount Paran.  
With him were myriads of holy ones;  
    at his right, a host of his own.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 3, 'Indeed, O favorite among peoples,  
    all his holy ones were in your charge;  
they marched at your heels,  
    accepted direction from you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 4, 'Moses charged us with the law,  
    as a possession for the assembly of Jacob.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 5, 'There arose a king in Jeshurun,  
    when the leaders of the people assembled--  
    the united tribes of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 6, 'May Reuben live, and not die out,  
    even though his numbers are few.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 7, 'And this he said of Judah:
O LORD, give heed to Judah,  
    and bring him to his people;  
strengthen his hands for him,  
    and be a help against his adversaries.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 8, 'And of Levi he said:
Give to Levi your Thummim,  
    and your Urim to your loyal one,  
whom you tested at Massah,  
    with whom you contended at the waters of Meribah;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 9, 'who said of his father and mother,  
    "I regard them not";  
he ignored his kin,  
    and did not acknowledge his children.  
For they observed your word,  
    and kept your covenant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 10, 'They teach Jacob your ordinances,  
    and Israel your law;  
they place incense before you,  
    and whole burnt offerings on your altar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 11, 'Bless, O LORD, his substance,  
    and accept the work of his hands;  
crush the loins of his adversaries,  
    of those that hate him, so that they do not rise again.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 12, 'Of Benjamin he said:
The beloved of the LORD rests in safety--  
the High God surrounds him all day long--  
    the beloved rests between his shoulders.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 13, 'And of Joseph he said:
Blessed by the LORD be his land,  
    with the choice gifts of heaven above,  
    and of the deep that lies beneath;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 14, 'with the choice fruits of the sun,  
    and the rich yield of the months;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 15, 'with the finest produce of the ancient mountains,  
    and the abundance of the everlasting hills;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 16, 'with the choice gifts of the earth and its fullness,  
    and the favor of the one who dwells on Sinai.  
Let these come on the head of Joseph,  
    on the brow of the prince among his brothers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 17, 'A firstborn bull--majesty is his!  
    His horns are the horns of a wild ox;  
with them he gores the peoples,  
    driving them to the ends of the earth;  
such are the myriads of Ephraim,  
    such the thousands of Manasseh.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 18, 'And of Zebulun he said:
Rejoice, Zebulun, in your going out;  
    and Issachar, in your tents.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 19, 'They call peoples to the mountain;  
    there they offer the right sacrifices;  
for they suck the affluence of the seas  
    and the hidden treasures of the sand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 20, 'And of Gad he said:
Blessed be the enlargement of Gad!  
    Gad lives like a lion;  
    he tears at arm and scalp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 21, 'He chose the best for himself,  
    for there a commander"s allotment was reserved;  
he came at the head of the people,  
    he executed the justice of the LORD,  
    and his ordinances for Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 22, 'And of Dan he said:
Dan is a lion"s whelp  
    that leaps forth from Bashan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 23, 'And of Naphtali he said:
O Naphtali, sated with favor,  
    full of the blessing of the LORD,  
    possess the west and the south.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 24, 'And of Asher he said:
Most blessed of sons be Asher;  
    may he be the favorite of his brothers,  
    and may he dip his foot in oil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 25, 'Your bars are iron and bronze;  
    and as your days, so is your strength.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 26, 'There is none like God, O Jeshurun,  
    who rides through the heavens to your help,  
    majestic through the skies.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 27, 'He subdues the ancient gods,  
    shatters the forces of old;  
he drove out the enemy before you,  
    and said, "Destroy!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 28, 'So Israel lives in safety,  
    untroubled is Jacob"s abode  
in a land of grain and wine,  
    where the heavens drop down dew.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(5, 'Ula', 'Deuteronomy', 33, 29, 'Happy are you, O Israel! Who is like you,  
    a people saved by the LORD,  
the shield of your help,  
    and the sword of your triumph!  
Your enemies shall come fawning to you,  
    and you shall tread on their backs.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);







"Cursed before the LORD be anyone who tries  
    to build this city--this Jericho!  
At the cost of his firstborn he shall lay its foundation,  
    and at the cost of his youngest he shall set up its gates!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 6, 27, 'So the LORD was with Joshua; and his fame was in all the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);




"Sun, stand still at Gibeon,  
    and Moon, in the valley of Aijalon."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 13, 'And the sun stood still, and the moon stopped,  
    until the nation took vengeance on their enemies.
Is this not written in the Book of Jashar? The sun stopped in midheaven, and did not hurry to set for about a whole day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 14, 'There has been no day like it before or since, when the LORD heeded a human voice; for the LORD fought for Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 15, 'Then Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, to the camp at Gilgal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 16, 'Meanwhile, these five kings fled and hid themselves in the cave at Makkedah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Five Kings Defeated'),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 17, 'And it was told Joshua, "The five kings have been found, hidden in the cave at Makkedah."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 18, 'Joshua said, "Roll large stones against the mouth of the cave, and set men by it to guard them;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 19, 'but do not stay there yourselves; pursue your enemies, and attack them from the rear. Do not let them enter their towns, for the LORD your God has given them into your hand."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 20, 'When Joshua and the Israelites had finished inflicting a very great slaughter on them, until they were wiped out, and when the survivors had entered into the fortified towns,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 21, 'all the people returned safe to Joshua in the camp at Makkedah; no one dared to speak against any of the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 22, 'Then Joshua said, "Open the mouth of the cave, and bring those five kings out to me from the cave."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 23, 'They did so, and brought the five kings out to him from the cave, the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, and the king of Eglon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 24, 'When they brought the kings out to Joshua, Joshua summoned all the Israelites, and said to the chiefs of the warriors who had gone with him, "Come near, put your feet on the necks of these kings." Then they came near and put their feet on their necks.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 25, 'And Joshua said to them, "Do not be afraid or dismayed; be strong and courageous; for thus the LORD will do to all the enemies against whom you fight."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 26, 'Afterward Joshua struck them down and put them to death, and he hung them on five trees. And they hung on the trees until evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 27, 'At sunset Joshua commanded, and they took them down from the trees and threw them into the cave where they had hidden themselves; they set large stones against the mouth of the cave, which remain to this very day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 28, 'Joshua took Makkedah on that day, and struck it and its king with the edge of the sword; he utterly destroyed every person in it; he left no one remaining. And he did to the king of Makkedah as he had done to the king of Jericho.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 29, 'Then Joshua passed on from Makkedah, and all Israel with him, to Libnah, and fought against Libnah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 30, 'The LORD gave it also and its king into the hand of Israel; and he struck it with the edge of the sword, and every person in it; he left no one remaining in it; and he did to its king as he had done to the king of Jericho.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 31, 'Next Joshua passed on from Libnah, and all Israel with him, to Lachish, and laid siege to it, and assaulted it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 32, 'The LORD gave Lachish into the hand of Israel, and he took it on the second day, and struck it with the edge of the sword, and every person in it, as he had done to Libnah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 33, 'Then King Horam of Gezer came up to help Lachish; and Joshua struck him and his people, leaving him no survivors.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 34, 'From Lachish Joshua passed on with all Israel to Eglon; and they laid siege to it, and assaulted it;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 35, 'and they took it that day, and struck it with the edge of the sword; and every person in it he utterly destroyed that day, as he had done to Lachish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 36, 'Then Joshua went up with all Israel from Eglon to Hebron; they assaulted it,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 37, 'and took it, and struck it with the edge of the sword, and its king and its towns, and every person in it; he left no one remaining, just as he had done to Eglon, and utterly destroyed it with every person in it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 38, 'Then Joshua, with all Israel, turned back to Debir and assaulted it,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 39, 'and he took it with its king and all its towns; they struck them with the edge of the sword, and utterly destroyed every person in it; he left no one remaining; just as he had done to Hebron, and, as he had done to Libnah and its king, so he did to Debir and its king.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 40, 'So Joshua defeated the whole land, the hill country and the Negeb and the lowland and the slopes, and all their kings; he left no one remaining, but utterly destroyed all that breathed, as the LORD God of Israel commanded.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 41, 'And Joshua defeated them from Kadesh-barnea to Gaza, and all the country of Goshen, as far as Gibeon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 42, 'Joshua took all these kings and their land at one time, because the LORD God of Israel fought for Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(6, 'Yos', 'Joshua', 10, 43, 'Then Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, to the camp at Gilgal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);















